From: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bootctrl: point misc device to mmcblk0p15

The dual-copy partition layout was changed in SDK v2.4.0: the firmware
partition was dropped, which shifted the misc partition from p17 to p15.
The misc device path is hardcoded, so it is updated to match the new
layout. Without this, open() on the non-existent /dev/mmcblk0p17 fails
and the boot slot can no longer be read or written.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
---
 bootctrl.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bootctrl.c b/bootctrl.c
--- a/bootctrl.c
+++ b/bootctrl.c
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 #define MISC_BOOT_CONTROL_VERSION 2
 #define COMMAND_LINE_SIZE 2048

-static const char *misc_device = "/dev/mmcblk0p17";
+static const char *misc_device = "/dev/mmcblk0p15";
 static const size_t SYNA_SPACE_OFFSET_IN_MISC = 4 * 1024;
 static const int kActiveSlotPriority = 8;
 static const int kOtherSlotPriority = 3;
